diagram "How a label reaches the page" version=1
subtitle "Three recent fixes, one per step"

config link-base="https://github.com/byronwall/draftably/"

# The labels point at footnotes ([1]); the footnotes carry the detail and link each PR.
node file "Source file" shape=pill color=sky
node compiler "Compiler"
node router "Router" color=violet
node renderer "Renderer" color=amber

edge m1 file -> compiler "label text"
edge m2 compiler -> compiler "wrap title lines evenly [1]"
edge m3 compiler -> router "boxes and label spots"
edge m4 router -> router "bring skip lines onto a diamond's top [2]"
edge m5 router -> renderer "routes"
edge m6 renderer -> renderer "paint label backgrounds [3]"

footnote 1 "[#436](pull/436) fits explicit title lines and wraps titles evenly."
footnote 2 "[#438](pull/438) brings a skip line onto a diamond's top, so lines do not cross."
footnote 3 "[#442](pull/442) draws each label's background in the surface under it, so a label in a tinted band keeps the band's tint."

layout root sequence
